# A local recording to its transcripts, through BCH's CUBE, in one play.
#
# Upload the recording into a folder of its own in ChRIS and run the Transcribe
# pipeline from that folder. chell roots a new feed on it with pl-dircopy, then
# pl-ffmpeg writes the audio as 16 kHz mono WAV and pl-whisper transcribes it
# on one of argentum's GPUs; the pipeline line returns when the feed has
# finished. The run's leaf, pl-whisper, is then downloaded: <name>.txt, .srt,
# .vtt, .tsv and .json under <OUT>/data/home_chris_uploads_transcribe_<LABEL>/,
# beside the run's jobs.jsonl. Needs a chell with leafPaths (mise#1364).
#
# Played from chell, logged in to the CUBE:
#
#     play examples/transcribe.mise --param AUDIO=~/meetings/weekly.mp4 --param LABEL=weekly-2026-11-03
#
# LABEL names the upload folder, ~/uploads/transcribe/<LABEL>; everything in
# it is transcribed, so a new recording takes a new label. OUT is where the
# transcripts land on the machine chell runs on. PIPELINE is the pipeline's
# /bin name on BCH's CUBE; another CUBE names it differently.
@name         Transcribe a recording
@description  Upload a local recording, run the Transcribe pipeline on it (pl-ffmpeg, then pl-whisper on a GPU), and download its transcripts.
@param        AUDIO
@param        LABEL
@param        OUT      = .
@param        PIPELINE = Transcribe_id293
@answers      RUN

mkdir -p ~/uploads/transcribe/${LABEL}
upload ${AUDIO} ~/uploads/transcribe/${LABEL}/
cd ~/uploads/transcribe/${LABEL}
RUN=$(${PIPELINE})
expect run ${RUN.leaves} status eq finishedSuccessfully
download ${RUN.leafPaths} ${OUT}
